  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Riligustilide may interact with the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is predicted to target several entities, including the Alpha-2A adrenergic receptor, which in turn is targeted by Cardanol, and Cardanol is also predicted to target the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B. Similarly, Riligustilide is predicted to interact with the Dopamine D4 receptor, which is targeted by Cardanol, and this receptor is also linked to the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B. These pathways indicate a potential mechanism by which Riligustilide could influence the 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2B, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across different scoring models, suggesting a plausible biological relationship, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
